<section class="outcomes" id="outcomes">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="kicker reveal">What changes</span>
      <h2 class="h2 reveal d1">Four things become true once you can see the whole system.</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div class="grid4">
      <div class="ocard reveal">
        <span class="mark"></span>
        <span class="idx">01</span>
        <h3>Capital sequenced in the right order</h3>
<p>
Which decisions have to land before others become explicit, so funding follows the dependency chain instead of fighting it.
</p>
   </div>
      
      <div class="ocard reveal d1">
        <span class="mark"></span>
        <span class="idx">02</span>
        <h3>Stranded-asset risk priced before you commit</h3>
      <p>
       Every proponent gets tested against the system it plugs into, so the exposure is visible while it&rsquo;s still time to change.
      </p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="ocard reveal d2">
        <span class="mark"></span>
        <span class="idx">03</span>
        <h3>Shared infrastructure costed across projects, not duplicated</h3>
        <p>Common-user facilities get sized for the precinct, not rebuilt four times over by four proponents who never spoke to each other.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="ocard reveal d3">
        <span class="mark"></span>
        <span class="idx">04</span>
        <h3>Governance designed before the concrete is poured</h3>
        <p>The authority to act on an opportunity exists at the point you find it, not two years and one stranded asset later.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
